{"base_rate":0.25895765472312704,"brier":0.18606970684039087,"bss":0.03037479853479852,"bss_hi":0.2304319351682783,"bss_lo":-0.19700527050018374,"chart":{"base":[397.8,76.6],"fp":[200.3,206.9],"lead":"62,229.7 272,203.5 482,174.6 692,111.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.03 — higher than 14% of cities","fp":"low end +0pp, high end +37pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.3 °C — better than 27% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 2%; promised 100% → rained 67%"},"rel":"64.1,458.9 255.9,406.8 600.7,276.3 691.6,175.7"},"country":"BR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.18967426710097723,"ess":307.9081398196911,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Sao Paulo</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Sao Paulo rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>67%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 614 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 9.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.03, ranked 184 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(136&ndash;200) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>242</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>59</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>78%</td><td class='num'><b>33%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>59</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>67%</b></td><td class='num'>125</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Sao Paulo</b> <span class=\"muted\">Brazil</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.03</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>136&ndash;200\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>614 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Sao Paulo &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Sao Paulo\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.184876033057854,377.4876033057851 108.54030769230769,298.0 231.28,159.89830508474574 333.345625,63.5 390.4,18.0 411.80176000000006,18.0 411.80176000000006,20.911999999999978 390.4,61.18644067796612 333.345625,137.4375 231.28,246.27118644067795 108.54030769230769,359.6 59.184876033057854,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"287.73941368078175\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"287.73941368078175\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.184876033057854,375.9834710743802 108.54030769230769,359.6 231.28,301.79661016949154 333.345625,262.5625 390.4,178.40677966101697 411.80176000000006,137.392\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 242 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.184876033057854\" cy=\"375.9834710743802\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 14%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 65 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"108.54030769230769\" cy=\"359.6\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 49%&amp;#10;It rained 22% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 59 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"231.28\" cy=\"301.79661016949154\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 78%&amp;#10;It rained 33% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"333.345625\" cy=\"262.5625\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 94%&amp;#10;It rained 56% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 59 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"390.4\" cy=\"178.40677966101697\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 67% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 125 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.80176000000006\" cy=\"137.392\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(26%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Sao Paulo the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>summer</b> (0.35) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.48).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>149</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>-0.481</td><td class='num'>38.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>135</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>0.052</td><td class='num'>14.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>151</td><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'>0.194</td><td class='num'>17.8%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'>0.347</td><td class='num'>7.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":-23.5475,"lon":-46.63611,"n":614,"n_cities":213,"name":"Sao Paulo","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.06,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.003347107438016529,"n":242,"obs":0.01652892561983471,"sig":true},{"hi":0.265,"lo":0.06,"mean":0.14276923076923076,"n":65,"obs":0.06153846153846154,"sig":false},{"hi":0.66,"lo":0.265,"mean":0.4894915254237288,"n":59,"obs":0.22033898305084745,"sig":true},{"hi":0.8820000000000005,"lo":0.66